1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,040
A whole camp is dying of snakebite — and God's

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,480
remedy is not to kill the snakes, or heal the

3
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,540
wounds, or hand out an antidote.

4
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:10,420
He tells them to look at a piece of metal on

5
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:10,800
a pole.

6
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:12,800
Look, and live.

7
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:16,240
It is one of the strangest cures in the Bible.

8
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,560
It happens near the end of the wilderness years.

9
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:22,240
Israel is worn down by the long road, and the

10
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:23,680
old bitterness boils over.

11
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:27,200
"Wherefore have ye brought us up out of Egypt

12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,980
to die in the wilderness?

13
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:32,720
for there is no bread, neither is there any

14
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:37,040
water; and our soul loatheth this light bread."

15
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:40,080
They have bread from heaven — and they despise

16
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,580
it, and accuse the God who has carried them

17
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:43,180
this far.

18
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:45,340
And then the ground itself turns against them.

19
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:48,460
"And the LORD sent fiery serpents among the

20
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:51,760
people, and they bit the people; and much people

21
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,660
of Israel died." Picture the camp.

22
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:57,960
The venom is already moving, and there is nothing

23
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,980
a bitten man can do to stop it — he cannot

24
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,260
run from a poison inside his own blood.

25
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,120
And notice what the people ask for.

26
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:09,160
They come to Moses and confess: "We have sinned,

27
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,100
for we have spoken against the LORD, and against

28
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:14,980
thee; pray unto the LORD, that he take away

29
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:17,880
the serpents from us." Their confession is

30
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:20,000
real — they name the sin itself.

31
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:23,680
But look at the cure they ask for: take away

32
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:25,720
the serpents, make the threat go away.

33
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:28,640
That would not save a single person already

34
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:31,640
bitten; the venom is already in the blood.

35
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,380
Even as they confess, their request reaches

36
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:36,860
only for the danger outside.

37
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:40,260
And that is the human problem in miniature:

38
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:44,240
we admit we have sinned, and still we beg God

39
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:47,500
mostly to change our circumstances — when the

40
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,420
poison is already within.

41
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:52,540
Now watch what God actually does — because

42
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:54,380
He does not do what they asked.

43
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:56,120
He does not take the serpents away.

44
00:01:56,860 --> 00:02:00,340
He says to Moses: "Make thee a fiery serpent,

45
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:03,320
and set it upon a pole: and it shall come to

46
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:05,680
pass, that every one that is bitten, when he

47
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:08,240
looketh upon it, shall live." Sit with how

48
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,220
strange that is.

49
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:12,780
The cure is shaped like the curse.

50
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:17,420
The thing lifted up is a serpent — a bronze

51
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:20,660
likeness of the very thing killing them — raised

52
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:22,300
on a pole for all to see.

53
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:25,740
God does not clear the serpents from the camp;

54
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:28,920
He turns the dying eye toward the image of

55
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,040
the judgment itself.

56
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:32,780
And the cure costs the bitten man nothing he

57
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:36,120
can boast in — not a potion to brew, not a

58
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:38,960
wound to lance, not a snake to fight.

59
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,440
"Every one that is bitten, when he looketh

60
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:43,720
upon it, shall live." One act.

61
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:45,140
Look.

62
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:48,820
"And Moses made a serpent of brass, and put

63
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:51,920
it upon a pole, and it came to pass, that if

64
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:55,120
a serpent had bitten any man, when he beheld

65
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:58,680
the serpent of brass, he lived." Now move forward

66
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,300
roughly fourteen hundred years, into a quiet

67
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:02,460
night-time conversation.

68
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:05,820
A religious leader named Nicodemus has come

69
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:08,080
to Jesus in the dark, trying to understand

70
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,000
who He is.

71
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:13,540
And Jesus reaches back — past the temple, past

72
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:16,300
the law — to a snake on a pole in the desert.

73
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:19,340
"And as Moses lifted up the serpent in the

74
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:22,560
wilderness, even so must the Son of man be

75
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:25,980
lifted up: That whosoever believeth in him

76
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:29,660
should not perish, but have eternal life."

77
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:30,840
Stop on that.

78
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:33,800
This is not a preacher centuries later finding

79
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,540
a clever picture in the Old Testament.

80
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:38,960
This is Jesus Himself, naming that pole as

81
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:40,640
a portrait of His own cross.

82
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:42,380
And He means it precisely.

83
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:46,020
Later, John tells us what that phrase pointed

84
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:49,960
to: "And I, if I be lifted up from the earth,

85
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:53,940
will draw all men unto me." John adds the note:

86
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:57,800
"This he said, signifying what death he should

87
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:00,420
die." "Lifted up" was the cross.

88
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:04,380
By Jesus' own word, the wilderness pole was

89
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:05,500
a picture of Calvary.

90
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:08,040
And the passage flows straight on into the

91
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:11,100
verse the whole world knows: "For God so loved

92
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:13,860
the world, that he gave his only begotten Son…"

93
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:16,940
The snake on the pole and "God so loved the

94
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:19,220
world" sit in the same breath of Scripture.

95
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:21,920
Now, be fair to the doubts, because there are

96
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:22,280
two.

97
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:25,520
First: doesn't a bronze snake on a pole just

98
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,320
become an idol?

99
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:30,640
Scripture itself answers that — bluntly.

100
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,620
Centuries later Israel did begin burning incense

101
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:37,300
to it, and a godly king named Hezekiah "brake

102
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:40,580
in pieces the brasen serpent that Moses had

103
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:44,020
made." The bronze never had power; God did.

104
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:48,940
Looking was never magic — it was trust, aimed

105
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:50,600
where God told them to aim it.

106
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:53,940
Scripture smashes the relic itself, so that

107
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:56,280
you never mistake the sign for the Savior.

108
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:59,920
Second, and deeper: isn't a serpent a strange

109
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:00,720
picture of Christ?

110
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:03,880
In the Bible the serpent is the tempter and

111
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:04,260
the curse.

112
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:08,620
Exactly — and that is the point, not the problem.

113
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,300
What hung on that pole was the likeness of

114
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:14,000
the very thing killing them; what hung on the

115
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,440
cross was the One of whom Scripture says God

116
00:05:16,440 --> 00:05:21,280
"hath made him to be sin for us, who knew no

117
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:24,840
sin" — the One "being made a curse for us:

118
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:28,740
for it is written, Cursed is every one that

119
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:31,820
hangeth on a tree." Christ did not become a

120
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:32,120
sinner.

121
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,440
He was lifted up bearing our curse, in the

122
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:38,260
likeness of the judgment we deserved — so the

123
00:05:38,260 --> 00:05:40,600
look of faith could find it there and live.

124
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:44,300
And this is not a stretch read into the text;

125
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:47,160
it is the meaning Jesus put there Himself.

126
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:49,200
So hold the two scenes together.

127
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:52,520
In the wilderness the cure was never in the

128
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:55,400
dying man — he could not neutralize the venom

129
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:57,100
or earn his way back to health.

130
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:00,780
It hung entirely outside him, on a pole.

131
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:01,760
That is the cross.

132
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:06,620
We are all bitten; the poison of sin is already

133
00:06:06,620 --> 00:06:09,360
in us, and no self-improvement reaches it.

134
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:14,120
So God lifted up His Son, who "his own self

135
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:17,580
bare our sins in his own body on the tree."

136
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,760
The curse fell on the lifted One, so that everyone

137
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,500
who looks to Him might live.

138
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:24,900
It cost the bitten Israelite nothing but a

139
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:25,680
turn of the eyes.

140
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,700
It cost the Son everything.

141
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:31,640
There is one more detail here, and it may be

142
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:35,100
the kindest of all: the cure was a look.

143
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:37,600
God could have asked for a climb, a payment,

144
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:38,940
a proof of strength.

145
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:42,340
He asked for the one thing a dying man can

146
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:42,900
still do.

147
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:47,140
You can be too weak to stand and still lift

148
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:47,680
your eyes.

149
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:51,080
The most poisoned person in the camp was no

150
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:53,680
further from healing than the least — both

151
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:56,720
were saved the same way, by looking away from

152
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,800
themselves to the One lifted up.

153
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:01,740
So the invitation is as wide as the word Jesus

154
00:07:01,740 --> 00:07:06,240
chose: "whosoever." You do not have to get

155
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:09,300
the poison out first, or feel strong, or be

156
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,820
certain your faith is large enough.

157
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,800
Faith is not a great work you produce; it is

158
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:17,040
the empty-handed look of someone who has stopped

159
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,360
trying to save themselves.

160
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:21,560
You only have to stop staring at the bite,

161
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:23,140
and look up.

162
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:25,760
The serpent in the wilderness was God teaching

163
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,860
the world one motion that saves.

164
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:31,840
He lifted His Son on a cross for exactly that

165
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:35,100
— so that whosoever turns their eyes to Him

166
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:38,600
"should not perish, but have eternal life."

167
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,640
You have stared at the bite long enough.

168
00:07:41,620 --> 00:07:44,280
The cure was never inside you — it is lifted

169
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:47,080
up, outside you, already finished.

170
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:50,580
Lift your eyes from the poison to the Saviour.

171
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:53,980
What He has done on that cross is enough.
